<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rudolf II, Holy Roman Emperor</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1552">1552</a>–<a href="/years/1612">1612</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rudolf II was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> ruler, King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> from 1572, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/king-of-bohemia">King of Bohemia</a> from 1575 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-emperor">Holy Roman Emperor</a> from 1576 to 1612. He moved his court to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague">Prague</a>, where he patronised artists and scholars such as Giuseppe Arcimboldo, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tycho-brahe">Tycho Brahe</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johannes-kepler">Johannes Kepler</a>. Withdrawn and unstable in later years, he was forced to yield Hungary, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> and finally <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a> to his brother Matthias.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rudolf-ii-holy-roman-emperor.jpg" alt="Rudolf II, Holy Roman Emperor" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Workshop of Martino Rota · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Martino_Rota_(workshop)_Portrait_of_Emperor_Rudolf.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>After 1526 the elected Habsburg kings gradually strengthened royal power, and <b>Rudolf II</b>, who made Prague his residence from 1583, granted religious freedom in the Letter of Majesty of 1609.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-bohemia">Kingdom of Bohemia · Governance &amp; Law</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1608, led by Karel the Elder of Žerotín, they sided with Archduke Matthias against Emperor <b>Rudolf II</b> and had their liberties confirmed.</blockquote><a href="/empire/margraviate-of-moravia">Margraviate of Moravia · Governance &amp; Law</a></li><li><blockquote>From the 1550s he rebuilt the village as a fortified ideal city, and Emperor <b>Rudolf II</b> made it a duchy in 1577.</blockquote><a href="/state/duchy-of-sabbioneta">Duchy of Sabbioneta</a></li></ul></section>
